d 'CGEMOD': module  for computable general equilibrium modelling, SAM balancing, microsimulation and scenario analysis
d
d  cgemod carries out a complete computable general equilibrium
d (CGE) study in Stata. It imports, audits, balances
d (sign-preserving cross-entropy/GRAS or RAS, with locked cells,
d reliability weights and control totals) and monitors social
d accounting matrices, and exports them to Excel, CSV or GAMS. It
d calibrates a standard single-country open-economy CGE model (CES
d value added, CET exports, Armington imports, multiproduct
d activities, home consumption, trade margins, Cobb-Douglas or LES
d demand) with alternative macro closures and factor-market
d regimes, including a wage curve, carbon taxes, quotas and price
d caps. It runs comparative-static and recursive-dynamic
d simulations with public and human capital and public debt, links
d results to household surveys for poverty and inequality analysis,
d performs systematic sensitivity analysis (Gaussian quadrature or
d Monte Carlo), and includes a scenario manager with Excel and HTML
d dashboard export. It also offers model diagnostics, a validation
d suite, Newton and Broyden solvers, and estimation of trade and
d substitution elasticities with residual diagnostics and remedies. d
d KW: computable general equilibrium
d KW: CGE
d KW: social accounting matrix
d KW: SAM
d KW: GRAS
d KW: cross entropy
d KW: Armington
d KW: microsimulation
d KW: poverty
d KW: sensitivity analysis
d KW: policy analysis
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261124
d
